{
  "version": "typed_evidence_gate_matrix_v1",
  "$comment": [
    "Every row is executed against all five gated transitions through their real",
    "production entry points, against a migrated database. The `expected` field is",
    "the assertion, never the source of truth: the test asserts the persisted",
    "proposal / signoff / epic row each transition would have written.",
    "",
    "`revision_offset` is how many spec revisions are committed AFTER the demand is",
    "raised. A finding's `demanded_revision_seq` is provenance, not a filter, so a",
    "demand must keep blocking as the head advances past it.",
    "",
    "`prose_only` rows additionally carry a Judge debate verdict whose prose asserts",
    "the claim is settled. Prose is not a disposition, so it must not unblock.",
    "",
    "`bypass` names a closure attempt made BEFORE the transitions run. Each is a",
    "path that used to look like it settled a demand while leaving",
    "`typed_evidence_findings.lifecycle` untouched:",
    "  generic_debate_resolve - resolve the needs_evidence debate row generically",
    "  advocate_disposition   - dispose of the finding as the Advocate, not the Judge",
    "  spike_task_closed      - close the linked spike to completed with no return",
    "Every bypass row still expects `blocked`.",
    "",
    "`expected_refusal` distinguishes the two fail-closed shapes. Closing the linked",
    "spike leaves the legacy compatibility link pointing at an inactive task, which",
    "the dual read has always treated as drift, so those rows are refused with the",
    "parity reason rather than the typed diagnostics. Both refuse; both leave the",
    "finding unresolved."
  ],
  "transitions": [
    "proposal_debate_append",
    "proposal_refinement_resolve",
    "proposal_signoff",
    "proposal_verdict_override",
    "proposal_graduate"
  ],
